But what about `_unwrapped_call(self.call)`? If `self.call` is a wrapped class, `_impartial(self.call)` might not be a class, but `_unwrapped_call(self.call)` might be.

Actually, `_impartial` just unwraps `partial`. `inspect.unwrap` unwraps decorators.

If `self.call` is a class, `_impartial(self.call)` is the class.

If `self.call` is a decorated class, `_impartial(self.call)` is the wrapper, and `_unwrapped_call(self.call)` is the class.

